{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg6mAzje63nQGEiGFjQjj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```regex\nhttps?://(?:[A-Za-z0-9-]+\\.)+[A-Za-z]{2,}(?::\\d{1,5})?(?:[/?#][^\\s<>\"']*)?\n```\n\n**How it works**\n- `https?://` matches the `http://` or `https://` scheme.\n- `(?:[A-Za-z0-9-]+\\.)+[A-Za-z]{2,}` matches the domain, such as `example.com` or `sub.example.co.uk`.\n- `(?::\\d{1,5})?` matches an optional port.\n- `(?:[/?#][^\\s<>\"']*)?` matches an optional path, query string or fragment, up to whitespace or a quote or angle bracket.\n\n**Example (Python)**\n```python\nimport re\npattern = re.compile(r'https?://(?:[A-Za-z0-9-]+\\.)+[A-Za-z]{2,}(?::\\d{1,5})?(?:[/?#][^\\s<>\"\\']*)?')\npattern.findall(\"Visit https://example.com/path?q=1 or http://foo.bar:8080/x#top.\")\n# ['https://example.com/path?q=1', 'http://foo.bar:8080/x#top.']\n```\n\n**Limitations**\n- It doesn't match `localhost`, IP addresses (`http://127.0.0.1`) or single-label hosts. To allow them, use `https?://[^\\s/$.?#][^\\s<>\"']*` instead. It's simpler and more permissive.\n- Trailing punctuation, like the `.` in the example, is included in the match. Strip it afterwards, or end the path part with `[^\\s<>\"'.,;:!?)]` if you want it excluded.\n- It checks the shape of a URL, not whether the URL is valid. For strict validation, use a URL parser such as `urllib.parse` or `new URL()`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6757,"cache_read_input_tokens":11227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6757},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9f12d12-4227-444d-a4c5-ebed9fe9653c","uuid":"b043915f-731e-4add-903b-47634fe589c6","timestamp":